first_claim:
Process to obtain mesenchymal cells with marked bone regenerative ability, which includes the following steps:
 a) isolating and expanding mesenchymal cells; 
 b) labeling said mesenchymal cells with suitable expression vectors; 
 c) positioning at least one scaffold; 
 d) inoculating said labeled cells in the circulatory system in at least one experimental model of bone damage; 
 e) removing the scaffold; 
 f) selecting said inoculated cells as concentrated in the damage site and expanding said selected cells in culture.

all_claims:
Process to obtain mesenchymal cells with marked bone regenerative ability, which includes the following steps:
 a) isolating and expanding mesenchymal cells; 
 b) labeling said mesenchymal cells with suitable expression vectors; 
 c) positioning at least one scaffold; 
 d) inoculating said labeled cells in the circulatory system in at least one experimental model of bone damage; 
 e) removing the scaffold; 
 f) selecting said inoculated cells as concentrated in the damage site and expanding said selected cells in culture.

Process according to claim 1  characterized in that :
 a) said isolation step involves isolation of adult human or animal mesenchymal cells, derived from tissues selected from bone marrow, tendons, muscle, adipose tissue; 
 b) said labeling step of said adult mesenchymal cells is achieved with lentiviral vector engineered with a protein that makes them fluorescent and selectable through antibiotic treatment; 
 c) said positioning of said scaffold is achieved in an experimental model of bone damage.

Process according to claim 1 and claim 2  characterized in that :
 a) said labeling of said adult mesenchymal cells is achieved with the Lentimax lentiviral vector engineered with the protein Green Fluorescent Protein (GFP) and gene for antibiotic resistance to puromycin; 
 b) said scaffold is a scaffold made of silicone tricalcium phosphate.
